From 5c8d71723bb06dd57fb8214f33ea5ae1a224b1de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:09:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/22] thingino: platform-enabling fixes and web UI platform
 flags

- thingino-isp pulls no Ingenic ISP stack on other vendors;
- thingino-ethernet selects the JZ MAC kernel options on Ingenic only;
- the control bar links "Photosensing Config" only with thingino-daynightd,
  and hides the motion controls and locks the speaker where the platform's
  web UI flags say so;
- the OSD page offers a stream restart instead of a reboot where the
  platform flag says a restart applies the OSD;
- the Sensor IQ page finds the sensor and its IQ file on SigmaStar
  (/etc/sensor/model; sensor-iq-name gives <sensor>.bin for the infinity*
  SoCs);
- the digital zoom bar's probe asks rvd for a non-zero crop window, so the
  bar stays off where rvd cannot zoom (no /proc/jz/sensor, as on SigmaStar)
  instead of failing on a click.

The flags default to the old behaviour. The SigmaStar values are set in
raptor-sigmastar.webui.json, in the streaming patch.
